The '''2026 Pune Municipal Corporation election''' was an election of members to the [[Pune Municipal Corporation]] which governs [[Pune]], the 7th largest [[List of metropolitan areas in India|metropolis]] in [[India]]. The election took place on 15 January 2026 and the counting took place on 16 January 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025 |title=Pune Municipal Corporation General Election Program 2025-26 |url=https://www.pmc.gov.in/en/b/pmc-general-election-program-2025-26 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260101081840/https://www.pmc.gov.in/en/b/pmc-general-election-program-2025-26 |archive-date=2026-01-01 |access-date=2026-01-01 |website=Pune Municipal Corporation}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Mutha |first=Snehal |date=2025-12-15 |title=Polls for BMC, 28 other municipal corporations on Jan. 15, vote count on Jan. 16 |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-maharashtra-municipal-corporation-election/article70398883.ece |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251217065949/https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/mumbai/mumbai-bmc-maharashtra-municipal-corporation-election/article70398883.ece |archive-date=2025-12-17 |access-date=2026-01-01 |work=The Hindu |language=en-IN |issn=0971-751X}}</ref> The [[Bharatiya Janata Party]] won a decisive victory winning 119 of the 168 seats.<ref>https://www.indiatvnews.com/maharashtra/pune-municipal-corporation-election-results-2026-live-bjp-vs-shinde-sena-vs-ncp-who-will-win-1025294</ref> BJP's Manjusha Nagpure was elected as the mayor and RPI(A)'s Parshuram Wadekar as the deputy mayor.

==Background==
After the Pune Municipal Corporation (PMC) elections of 2017, the city was divided into 41 administrative wards, electing a total of 162 corporators, with each ward returning four members. As per the latest ward formation and reservation draft notification issued by the Government of Maharashtra, The city is divided into 41 wards(प्रभाग). 40 wards are represented by 4 corporators(नगरसेवक) each, while 1 ward(No. 38) is represented by 5 corporators. Thus, the general body consists of 165 elected councilors or corporators. All major political parties active in the state, contest the elections.

